> From 217219cc2d3cafe109f2b0a00ac4474e680fe391 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
> From: Jiri Pirko <jiri@nvidia.com>
> Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:50:36 +0200
> Subject: [PATCH 03/20] ctlv: Add the root family specification and generated
>  files
>
> Define the root family used by every CTLV device. Add its ABI snapshot,
> registry and manifest entries, and generated outputs.
>
> The generated kernel descriptor is preparatory and is linked after its
> handlers arrive with device and operation dispatch.

Bisectability: this changelog admits the generated .c is not linked, but it understates the problem. `include/linux/ctlv_gen.h` (outside the `_CTLV_GENERATED_METADATA_ONLY` guard) uses `CTLV_IN_REF`/`CTLV_IN_HAS`/`CTLV_IN_U64`/`CTLV_IN_FOR_EACH` (only added by patch 5), `CTLV_PUT_*`/`CTLV_NEST_START` and `CTLV_EVENT_CREATE` (builder/event patches), and `drivers/ctlv/ctlv_gen.c` refers to `ctlv_op_pre()`, `ctlv_priv_size()`, `ctlv_families_dump_query()` etc. that do not exist before the dispatch patch. Nothing compiles `ctlv_gen.h` (no Makefile/Kconfig yet), so after this patch nothing proves the generated output is even syntactically valid C; it only becomes so ~8 patches later. Also `drivers/ctlv/` is added to MAINTAINERS only in patch 5, so this patch creates `drivers/ctlv/ctlv_gen.c` outside any F: entry.

