> +  # The nest carried by every family blob attr. va uses address; fd and offset

Speculative generality frozen into the UAPI: blob.fd and blob.offset are "reserved for later fd-backed types", blob-type has the single value "va", and schema.blob-backings is a bitmask over that single value. Nothing in the series reads or writes blob.fd/blob.offset, yet they get attr IDs 3 and 4 forever (and fd has a max with no semantics). If fd-backed blobs come later, they can be appended as new IDs then; reserving IDs speculatively adds dead put-helpers (`ctlv_blob_fd`/offset) and ABI-snapshot entries to maintain.

> +  # are reserved for later fd-backed types.
> +  - name: blob
> +    attrs:
> +      - name: type
> +        enum: blob-type
> +      - name: address
> +        type: uint
> +      - name: fd
> +        type: uint
> +        max: 2147483647
> +      - name: offset
> +        type: uint
> +      - name: length
> +        type: uint
> +        min: 1
> +
> +  # Error information: only what describes the first failure is present.

error-info (attr-set) makes every member optional, including error.reason, so a message with no reason at all is schema-valid. If reason is always emitted it should be required, otherwise a client cannot rely on it. Also the comment says "first failure", but the error group/attr-set carries no indication of whether more failures were suppressed; fine, just make sure the docs say first-failure-wins.

