subscriptions-add/-remove and event-queue-set are state-changing actions declared fd-access: read. This is deliberate for per-open state but it means a read-only open can resize its event queue up to 16 MiB (event.queue-len max 16777216). Please state in the comment/doc that per-open state is considered not to need write access, and confirm the queue allocation is memcg accounted and rlimit-bounded, since a bound of 16 MiB per open fd is cheap to multiply.

