Summary of the most serious issues in this patch:
- Series bisectability: the generated kernel header/source depend on macros and functions from patches 5-11 and are not compiled by anything until dispatch lands; `drivers/ctlv/ctlv_gen.c` is not covered by MAINTAINERS until patch 5.
- Registry/manifest entries are added before the implementation, contradicting `families.yaml`'s own rule.
- Linux-syscall-note SPDX on non-UAPI kernel files (`ctlv_gen.c`, `linux/ctlv_gen.h`).
- Speculative ABI: reserved blob.fd/blob.offset, single-value blob-type, error.reason optional.
- Generator output nits: duplicate extern `ctlv_family`, `_present()` for required attrs, underscore-prefixed UAPI identifiers.
